  next_durable_transition: Preserve all closed bytes. Diagnose model load under a new bounded diagnostic identity, add a generic failing test, correct cleanly, gate/commit/push/fresh-verify, then preregister wholly new execution identities. Never invoke or mutate the closed operation.

ledger_2026_08_26_scalar_numerical_probe_checkpoint:
  durable_record: wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-scalar-numerical-probe-memory-2026-08-26.md, 11,886 bytes, SHA256 2f5b59074e000f2f87b6e04b4150032581469fb4df0fae2a5ef4ad7f1ee52a01.
  accepted_design: A non-shipping leaf probe consumes a strict canonical private request, verifies exact model bytes before output, calls the existing scalar traced path once per registered token, creates bounded f32le packs create-only, preserves partial failure evidence, and writes probe.json last. It adds no reader, sampler, fallback, retry, repair, or production dispatch.
  report_lineage: The durable record links the post-/10 intake manifest, corrected synthesis, TDD delta, and intake memory. Adopted conclusions are the three-arrow numerical proof, strict input-layer identity, preregistered tensor-class thresholds, first-divergence localization, and immutable failure custody.
  verification_truth: Focused checks pass; full standard is 1,515/0/2. Commit 8b140ec/tree a40150e is pushed and fresh-four-way exact. Clean run 8c483720 passed 23/23; 3,995-byte aggregate a0bb5bb7 independently verifies. Real Qwen3, source framework, quantization noninferiority, scalar parity, optimized kernels, and browser WASM remain unobserved.
  next_durable_transition: Record a source-framework/probe/verifier implementation checkpoint, then separately register one all-new output-free numerical operation. Never turn this implementation ledger entry into execution evidence.
